:: Best Ending [ending todo] {"position":"2000,290","size":"100,100"}
!Best Ending
The power plant survives and the MC has named the conspirators (at least Elvira on the human side and two of the King, Dench and the Watch plant) with proof or witnesses. The Atlantean press reports it, Aishui and Seayssal revoke the King's mandate together, and a peaceful revolution ends the monarchy. Honest Council members extradite the corrupt ones to stand trial with the Atlanteans; the guilty are sentenced to work at the Wellness Retreat. Epilogue: the Council and Atlantis build greener tech together, the retreat opens spas around Atlantis, Castella becomes minister of public health, the Bleaching slowly fades, and the Leviathan seeds new special coral.

Aishui revokes the King's mandate, backed by Seayssal. Elvira is exposed as the human conspirator. Castella becomes health minister.
/* TODO: Elvira is never introduced in Acts 1 to 4. Seed her somewhere. */
[[Codex]]


:: Good Ending [ending todo] {"position":"2000,410","size":"100,100"}
!Good Ending
The power plant survives but the MC can't prove exactly who was involved. The general cover-up still comes out, Aishui revokes the King's mandate with the Leviathan's support, and the new government bans the Council from Atlantis. The MC may stay as the new contact while Sir Richard returns to reform the Council. Epilogue: like the best ending but without the Council or surface reforms; the MC either settles in Atlantis or returns to found an independent research group with Sir Richard.

Aishui revokes the King's mandate with Seayssal's support. Castella becomes health minister. The Atlantean conspirators (King, Dench, Watch plant) are named.


:: Bad Ending [ending todo] {"position":"2000,530","size":"100,100"}
!Bad Ending
The power plant was blown up. District 5 faces heavy cleanup. The corruption is exposed in general terms, but Atlanteans resent that Sir Richard decided for them when they could have dismantled the plant more cleanly. The MC and Sir Richard return to the surface to found their own research organization, free of the Council.

